# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the monthly-expense-tracker React + Vite application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1
- **Method**: Installed using npm (project's package manager)
- **Files Updated**: 
  - `package.json` - Added `@vercel/analytics` to dependencies
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies

### 2. Analytics Integration
- **File Modified**: `client/src/App.jsx`
- **Changes**:
  1. Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
  2. Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main App component's JSX (before the closing `</div>`)

### 3. Implementation Details
Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- Used the React-specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Placed the Analytics component in the root App component to track all page interactions
- The component is self-contained and requires no additional props or configuration

### 4. Testing & Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ All dependencies resolved correctly
- ✅ No breaking changes introduced
- ✅ Lock files properly updated

## Next Steps
To enable analytics data collection:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify tracking by checking browser's Network tab for fetch/XHR requests to `/<unique-path>/view`
4. Access analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after users visit the site

## Technical Notes
- Framework: React 18.3.1 with Vite 5.4.9
- Analytics Package Version: @vercel/analytics@2.0.1
- The Analytics component is lightweight and has minimal performance impact
- No additional configuration required for basic tracking
- Analytics will only be active when deployed on Vercel's platform
